w: 1.~My hope is built on no- thing less Than Je- sus' blood and right- eous- ness; I dare not trust the sweet- est frame, But whol- ly lean on Je- sus' name. _ On _ Christ, the sol- id _ Rock, I stand; All _ o- ther ground is _ sin- king sand, All _ o- ther ground is _ sin- king sand. _
w: 2.~When dark- ness veils his love- ly face, I rest up- on un- chang- ing grace; In ev'- ry rough and storm- y gale My an- chor holds with- in the veil. _ On _ Christ, the sol- id _ Rock, I stand; All _ o- ther ground is _ sin- king sand, All _ o- ther ground is _ sin- king sand. _
w: 3.~His oath, his cov- e- nant, his blood Sup- port me in the whelm- ing flood; When all a- round my soul gives way, He then is all my hope and stay. _ On _ Christ, the sol- id _ Rock, I stand; All _ o- ther ground is _ sin- king sand, All _ o- ther ground is _ sin- king sand. _
w: 4.~When I shall launch in worlds un- seen, O may I then be found in him; Dressed in his right- eous- ness a- lone, Fault- less to stand be- fore the throne. _ On _ Christ, the sol- id _ Rock, I stand; All _ o- ther ground is _ sin- king sand, All _ o- ther ground is _ sin- king sand. _
